-- #3726 — `.x` on a receiver of type `T`, whose two constructors both declare `x`
-- at the SAME position but with different types.  The slot agrees, so the
-- position test alone accepted it; the access is typed by the selected
-- constructor's declaration with no tag test, and the built binary printed a
-- `String`'s heap address as an `Int` for a `B` value at exit 0.  A field must
-- have one type across every constructor that holds it; this one must reject.
data T = A { x : Int } | B { x : String }

getX : T -> Int
getX v = v.x
